issue.description:
Refine the music-player gallery composition so the slider thumb uses the semantic primary color and the five transport controls share one consistent visual treatment.

1. Slider thumb

Owner direction:

* Change the progress/seek slider thumb so its visible circular fill uses the semantic primary background token.
* Prefer the accepted equivalent of bg-primary for the thumb fill.
* Preserve an appropriate border/focus treatment for contrast and accessibility.

Preserve:

* current slider track styling;
* elapsed/remaining labels;
* current progress interaction;
* keyboard/focus behavior;
* light/dark behavior.

2. Play/Pause button treatment

Remove the current special large filled-circle treatment from Play/Pause.

Make Play/Pause use the same overall button treatment as:

* Shuffle;
* Previous;
* Next;
* Repeat.

Requirements:

* same visual weight;
* same button/touch-target size;
* same general surface treatment;
* same spacing rhythm;
* keep Play/Pause functionality and state switching.

The five controls should read as one consistent transport-control row rather than having Play/Pause dominate visually.

3. Solid icon variants

Audit the project's current icon library for legitimate solid/filled variants of:

* Shuffle;
* Previous;
* Play;
* Pause;
* Next;
* Repeat.

If solid/filled variants are available:

* prefer them for the music-control row;
* keep icon sizing consistent.

If the current icon library does not provide legitimate solid variants:

* keep the existing official icon variants;
* do not invent custom filled SVGs solely for this card;
* do not add a new icon dependency just for this request unless source inspection proves it is already justified elsewhere.

Preserve:

* current control order: Shuffle / Previous / Play-Pause / Next / Repeat;
* equal-sized touch targets;
* even distribution across the row;
* accessible names for icon-only controls;
* current lightweight local playback state;
* semantic-token styling;
* stable card geometry.

Do not:

* change music-player placement/order;
* change song metadata/content;
* change timeline-label typography/position from the accepted state;
* add real audio/network behavior;
* add new public resources;
* change unrelated gallery compositions.

Acceptance:

* Slider thumb visibly uses the semantic primary background token.
* Play/Pause no longer has the special oversized filled-circle treatment.
* Play/Pause matches the other four transport controls in size and visual treatment.
* All five control targets remain equal-sized and evenly distributed.
* Solid icon variants are used when genuinely available in the existing icon library.
* No fake/custom solid SVGs are introduced if such variants are unavailable.
* Playback interaction, keyboard/focus accessibility, light/dark behavior, and stable geometry remain intact.
